| `scripts/launch.py` | Decides where a long script runs and runs it, and is the one writer of the duration record; `scripts/long_scripts.py` imports its config loader and record reader, so the proposal and the decision read the block by one rule. | `python3 scripts/launch.py -- make verify` | [`launcher.farm.adapter`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Not a scheduler: no queue, no retry. load_launcher_config checks the load threshold range before math.isfinite, so oversized integers exit CONFIG naming launcher.spare.max_load_per_cpu; booleans, non-finite floats and out-of-range numbers remain refusals. The `launcher` row below is the feature this module carries. | [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
